{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfv1XPqM68nGnyKfkCeJc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `tests/test_agent.py` and all 321 tests pass with the command you gave. The library code is unchanged; `git status` shows only the new `tests/` folder and a `__pycache__` that running the tests created.\n\n**What it covers:**\n- **Basics:** whole-string matching (a trailing newline is rejected), unnamed and named fields, `{{`/`}}` escapes, regex special characters in the literal text, case sensitivity, newlines inside fields, the `Result` lookups and `repr`.\n- **Named fields:** dotted names like `{a.b}`, names with hyphens and underscores (including clashes such as `{a.b}` with `{a_b}`), dict-style names like `{a[b][c]}`, repeated names that must match the same value, and `RepeatedNameError`.\n- **Spans:** start/end positions, including fields that come after types which add their own internal regex groups.\n- **Numbers:**\n  - `d`: signs, `0x`/`0o`/`0b` prefixes, `,` and `_` grouping, width\n  - `b`/`o`/`x`/`X`/`n`/`%`\n  - `f`/`F` (`F` returns `Decimal`), including `.0f`, plus `e`/`g`, nan and inf\n  - `int_convert` tested directly\n- **Text types and padding:** `w W s S D l`, width and precision, `< > ^ =` alignment, custom fill characters (including regex specials), and round trips through `str.format`.\n- **Dates and times:** all eight built-in date/time types (`ti te tg ta th tc tt ts`), with AM/PM (including 12 AM/PM), microseconds and every time-zone offset form. Also strftime-style formats like `{:%Y-%m-%d}` returning a `date`, `datetime` or `time`, and `FixedTzOffset`.\n- **Other:** custom types via `extra_types` and `with_pattern` (including patterns that contain their own groups), `search`/`findall` with `pos`/`endpos`, `evaluate_result=False`, and `Parser` properties and `repr`.\n\n**Checking it catches bugs:** I planted 43 single bugs, one at a time, in a throwaway copy of the library and ran the suite against each. The first run caught 40. I added tests for two of the misses; the third mutant behaves the same as the original, so no test can tell them apart. Final score: 42 of 43. I deleted the copy afterwards.\n\n**Things you might not expect (the tests check the current behaviour):**\n- **Width on text fields keeps the padding.** `{:10}` means \"at least 10 characters\", so parsing `\"       abc\"` gives `\"       abc\"`, not `\"abc\"`. Use `{:>}` without a width to strip the padding.\n- **`{:d}` counts a leading space as a sign.** Searching for `{:d}` in `\"abc 123\"` gives a span that includes the space.\n- **Likely bugs that I left untested** (each one is a single line in `parse/__init__.py`):\n  - A regex-special fill with `=` alignment, like `{:*=8.2f}`, crashes with `NotImplementedError`. The fill is put into the pattern before it gets escaped (line 836).\n  - A non-zero fill with `=` on a float, like `{:#=8.2f}`, raises `ValueError`, because the fill is captured along with the number. It works for `d`, where non-digits are stripped before converting.\n  - A dict key containing a space, like `{a[b c]}`, raises `NotImplementedError`, because the space can't go into a regex group name."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":348,"cache_read_input_tokens":67998,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":348},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9829a8c7-2507-4c3b-8a56-496094d68db1","uuid":"9b29e45c-3e45-460d-b034-a141fcfca2dd","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:53:59.975Z","request_id":"req_011Cfv1XPVkb3jzYdTnrMDZG"}
